{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 3eda74ed8342f881f9d2e69b2b25ac99cdca01b7 on planner/cutover-plan-20261114, both artifacts, for request dc343d96 under promise d637fac5 and review request dbfa5c6d. The plan holds against main 4cef11d2. This approval is the review that `docs/deploy.md` asks for of the three `--var` overrides that the note names: `REGISTER_SCOPE`, the `registerScope` field of `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG`, and `INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES` on `dap-demo`. It covers no other override.\n\nThe four points of the request:\n\n1. The three facts hold.\n   - A plan lives 840 s. `command-install.ts:196` and `:226` sign with `PROPOSED_BOUNDS.intentLifetimeSeconds - 60`, and `contract/src/bounds.ts:80` sets the lifetime to `15 * 60`.\n   - I did not trace the 900 s read of a `keys` register to its line. It is a second bound of the same intent lifetime, and the plan already keeps the install and `dap create` inside one 14-minute window.\n   - `git diff 64112e45 4cef11d2` touches none of the three `migrations` blocks. Lending and Grow each change one line (`PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS`, now with the base pins first). Demo changes the same line, removes `DEMO_START_CONFIG` and changes a comment.\n2. The three overrides are enough for the window. At main, the tracked files name a register in four settings: `REGISTER_SCOPE`, `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG`, `INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES` (demo only), and the old Grow directory in `APPLICATION_SCREEN_HOSTS` and `GROW_ARCHIVE_CONFIG`. The note keeps the last two on purpose until head C and precondition 4. `PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS` already admits the base pins on all three Workers, so a register of `platform:register@28` needs no other change. `DEMO_START_CONFIG` is absent at main, so the demo offer answers 404 as the note says.\n3. The fault table and the rollback rule are right. A Workers version holds its code and its variables, so `wrangler rollback` brings back the old register, and with no migration the old code reads its own objects. Rolling back only before `dap create` succeeds is the right line: after it, the new room holds acts that the old version cannot serve.\n4. A deployment of the tracked files after the window points each Worker at a retired register. The tracked `REGISTER_SCOPE` and `ARTIFACTS_CONFIG` still name `sc_c67lq575…` (Lending), `sc_yatkl7ku…` (Grow) and `sc_zm56yco5…` (demo), and `deploy.mjs` deploys the file alone. Head A must land before `deploy.mjs` runs for those three Workers.\n\nWhat I checked: main 4cef11d2 is the head's only parent, and the head changes the two paths that the two artifacts cover. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, the commit-message check passes (1 checked, 0 flagged), and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran nothing against a Worker and read no Cloudflare state. I did not read the runbook outside the head.\n\nArchitecture: sound. One Worker at a time, Lending first because no visitor uses it, and a stop before `dap-demo` on any fault. The window changes values that a reviewed head will track, and head A records them.\n\nSecurity: the window changes the register that each public Worker trusts, and this review cannot bind the new scope IDs, because the plan creates them inside the window. What binds them is the operator's own plan, signed in a fresh home under a 0700 root, with `REGISTER_SCOPE` set to the planned scope. Another key cannot install a register at that scope ID. The END act must therefore record, for each Worker, the scope and genesis that the plan printed and the same scope in `/health`, as step 7 says. Head A then puts those values under review. On `dap-demo`, the register is `open` from the install on, as the note intends.\n\nThree notes, none blocking:\n\n1. In the template, `--var INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES:[\"$REG\"]` sits inside a double-quoted shell argument, so its inner quotes need escaping or single quotes around the JSON. The step 1 dry run will show it. Write the exact command in the runbook before the window.\n2. I did not trace how `indexedScopes` (`scope/src/scope-index.ts:76-130`) admits the first create of a new register in `enforce` mode. The note puts Lending first, and its fault table rolls back on \"not found\", so a refusal there stops the plan before Grow and demo.\n3. Only the note stops `deploy.mjs` for `grow`, `lending` and `demo` between the window and head A. Say so in the END act, and in the builder's hold if the builder holds a deployment.\n\nThis approval authorizes the window as written once CDF-1 is on main. It authorizes no landing, and the planner lands the note.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:72ee883b27248a1b3ab8b3037e0583c898fd7ebd","binding":"assigned","head":"3eda74ed8342f881f9d2e69b2b25ac99cdca01b7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c28eb828ae9b05a7325826bbba2db9bbdeea1e07\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d637fac54ded750da3d042c1f51c536395e5af5b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f33f0b869a64490c92e79a30a3080a5cea11f0ac","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}